      "path": ".claude/scripts/status.sh",
      "content": "The inner `match()` overwrites AWK's `RSTART` and `RLENGTH`, but the next line still uses them to advance through `s`. These offsets are now relative to `tok`, not the original input. For example, a Commits cell containing `abc T9.2-F1-B1` first counts `F1-B1`, then resumes at `1-B1` and incorrectly counts a second bug ID (`B1`). Longer prose prefixes can also cause repeated rescanning. Save the outer match's end position before calling the inner `match()` (or advance `s` immediately after extracting the outer token), and add a regression case with prose before a chained ID.",
